# Example 04: the target/binder convention.
# PDB 5VW1, SpCas9(D10A/H840A)-sgRNA bound by the phage anti-CRISPR
# protein AcrIIA4, which occupies the PAM-recognition site.
# Yang & Patel 2017, Mol Cell 67:117.
#
# Rule from BindCraft: the given thing is a neutral surface, the thing the
# panel is about is a saturated cartoon. Two colors, not ten.
#
# Chain IDs here are not the obvious ones: A = Cas9, B = AcrIIA4,
# C = sgRNA. Always run "info chains" before writing selections.
open 5vw1
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

# Target: Cas9 as a neutral surface, slightly transparent so the binder
# stays visible where it packs against the protein
surface /A
color /A lab_gray_p target s
transparency /A 25 target s
hide /A cartoons

# sgRNA present but quiet
color /C lab_gray target acf

# Binder: the only saturated color in the panel
color /B lab_vermillion
cartoon style /B xsection oval width 2.0 thickness 0.6

view
turn y 270
view pad 0.05

2dlabels text "SpCas9" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_gray bold true
2dlabels text "sgRNA" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.89 size 22 color lab_gray bold true
2dlabels text "AcrIIA4" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.84 size 22 color lab_vermillion bold true
2dlabels text "5VW1" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.04 size 18 color lab_gray

save binder_target.png width 3000 supersample 3
